            <ArticleTitle>Entrapment of angiographic catheter in the right coronary artery: a trap for the nonexperienced operator.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>75-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of angiographic catheter entrapment in the right coronary artery during coronary angiography in a patient with excessive tortuosity of the right iliac artery is described. Alternative manipulations in order to avoid this problem are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
